;; analyses.decl: the facts a rule guard may ask about a class.
;;
;;   (analysis NAME (params) :type T :spec S)
;;   (pred     NAME (params) :uses A :spec S)
;;
;; The :spec is a boolean expression over the parameters and the builtins. It is the hypothesis of every
;; proof obligation and the sampler of the generated fuzz: `(bool01 x)` samples x in {0, 1}. A guard on an
;; analysis compiles to a call of the runtime implementation (rulegen's analysis table); rulegen refuses a
;; guard whose analysis the runtime does not implement yet.
;;
;; Milestone G adds range, known bits, nonneg, range_bounded and known_zero_outside here, each with its
;; implementation in pass/aegraph/analyses/.

(analysis bool01 (x) :type bool :spec (and (<= 0 x) (<= x 1)))
